    "## 1. Load the dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The bizbrains corpus ships as three Parquet shards, one per split. We read all three and\n",
    "concatenate them into a single DataFrame, tagging each row with a `split` column so the\n",
    "original train / validation / test assignment survives the merge.\n",
    "\n",
    "Working with one frame keeps every later check consistent — the same duration logic, the same\n",
    "silence thresholds, the same flags apply across all splits — while `split` lets us group back\n",
    "out whenever a per-split view matters.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expect:** 979 rows × 4 columns (`audio`, `text`, `speaker_gender`, `split`)."
   ]
