   "source": [
    "### Duration summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The distribution that decides whether the data fits Whisper's input constraints.\n",
    "\n",
    "Whisper's encoder always consumes a fixed 30-second window: shorter audio is zero-padded to\n",
    "3000 mel frames, and **anything longer is silently truncated while the full transcript is kept\n",
    "as the label**. That combination trains the model to emit text for audio it never heard, which\n",
    "is a direct path to hallucination and run-on output at inference. So the number that matters\n",
    "most here is the maximum.\n",
    "\n",
    "A useful corollary: because everything pads to 30 s, compute cost per sample is identical\n",
    "regardless of clip length. Short clips are not cheaper — they are just less data per step."
   ]
