    "### Level report and flagging\n",
    "\n",
    "Turning the continuous measurements into a small set of boolean flags, then counting them.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each threshold marks a different failure mode: `near_silent` catches recordings that essentially\n",
    "failed; `very_quiet` catches level outliers that are still usable; `clipped` catches distortion;\n",
    "`mostly_silence` and the lead/trail flags catch bad segment boundaries.\n",
    "\n",
    "The key interpretive distinction is **fix versus drop**:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Many clips flagged for lead/trail silence, but the speech itself is clean → systematic\n",
    "  segmentation slack. Fix with a trimming step in preprocessing; do not delete.\n",
    "- Many flagged `very_quiet` but intelligible → fix with loudness normalisation; do not delete.\n",
    "- A few clips where audio and transcript genuinely do not correspond → drop those.\n",
    "\n",
    "With ~2.5 hours available, the bias should be strongly toward fixing. `n_flags` sums the conditions\n",
    "per clip so the worst offenders sort to the top for manual audition."
   ]
  },
