    "# 6. Cross-checking silence with VAD\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything above decided \"silence\" from a single absolute energy threshold (`-45 dBFS`). That is\n",
    "fast and dependency-free, but it has a known blind spot: it measures **loudness**, not **speech**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two failure modes follow directly from that:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **False silence.** A quietly recorded but perfectly intelligible clip falls below the threshold\n",
    "  and is reported as mostly silent. We would trim or drop real speech.\n",
    "- **False speech.** Steady background noise — air conditioning, hum, room tone, music — sits above\n",
    "  the threshold, so the energy method calls it voiced. Leading silence is reported as ~0 s when\n",
    "  there is really a second of noise before anyone speaks.\n",
    "\n",
    "A Voice Activity Detector decides speech versus non-speech from *spectral structure* rather than\n",
    "level, so it fails in genuinely different ways. That independence is the whole point: where the two\n",
    "methods agree we can trust the measurement, and where they disagree we have a shortlist of clips\n",
    "worth listening to.\n",
    "\n",
