    "### 6.2 Compare the two methods\n",
    "\n",
    "Joining the VAD results onto `lv` and computing the per-clip difference between the two estimates.\n",
    "\n",
    "Read these summary numbers as follows:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Correlation near 1.0** — the two methods agree on the overall picture, and the energy-based\n",
    "  numbers from section 5 can be trusted.\n",
    "- **A consistent positive or negative bias** — the methods disagree systematically, which usually\n",
    "  means the `-45 dBFS` threshold is mis-set for this corpus rather than that individual clips are\n",
    "  broken. If VAD consistently reports *more* silence, there is background noise sitting above the\n",
    "  energy threshold; if it reports *less*, the threshold is cutting into quiet speech.\n",
    "- **High spread with low bias** — they agree on average but disagree per clip, which is the case\n",
    "  where individual clips genuinely need auditioning."
   ]
  },
