    "### 6.3 Visualise the agreement\n",
    "\n",
    "Scatter plots put each clip on both axes with the dashed line marking perfect agreement, which\n",
    "makes the *shape* of any disagreement visible in a way summary statistics cannot.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Points tight on the diagonal → the methods agree.\n",
    "- A cloud consistently **above** the line → VAD finds more silence than energy did, i.e. noise was\n",
    "  being counted as speech.\n",
    "- A cloud consistently **below** → VAD finds less silence, i.e. quiet speech was being counted as\n",
    "  silence.\n",
    "- A few scattered outliers with the bulk on the diagonal → those specific clips are the ones to\n",
    "  listen to.\n",
    "\n",
    "The fourth panel plots the distribution of speech-time disagreement in seconds, which is the most\n",
    "directly interpretable version: how many seconds of each clip the two methods argue about."
   ]
