    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. What this tells us, and what comes next\n",
    "\n",
    "Pulling the observation phase together into decisions:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Format** — if every clip is already 16 kHz mono PCM_16, the pipeline needs no resampling and\n",
    "   no format conversion, so there is no quality loss from preprocessing.\n",
    "2. **Duration** — with no clip approaching the 30 s window, no truncation risk exists and no\n",
    "   filtering on length is required beyond a defensive `< 29 s` guard.\n",
    "3. **Transcript integrity** — the chars-per-second, empty-text, duplicate, and language checks\n",
    "   above give a shortlist to fix or drop. Fix where the audio is intact; the corpus is too small to\n",
    "   delete liberally.\n",
    "4. **Silence and level** — the energy-versus-VAD comparison decides whether a trimming step is\n",
    "   needed at all, and which measurement should drive it.\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing pipeline that follows should then run in this order, each step reducing work for\n",
    "the next: text normalisation (NFC, ZWJ policy, digits, punctuation, whitespace) → row filtering →\n",
    "optional silence trimming and loudness normalisation → feature extraction with\n",
    "`WhisperFeatureExtractor` (80 mel bins for `small`) and `WhisperTokenizer(language=\"sinhala\",\n",
    "task=\"transcribe\")` → a collator that pads features and pads labels with `-100`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two things worth doing before any training run. First, verify that no transcript exceeds the\n",
    "decoder's 448-token limit after tokenisation, since Sinhala tokenises inefficiently. Second,\n",
    "evaluate un-fine-tuned `whisper-small` on this test split to get a baseline WER — it costs minutes\n",
    "and makes the fine-tuning result interpretable rather than just a number."
